From 96fbc35a4865ad506a732ca8a9c25f9a09d4200b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soundSHINE Bot <bot@soundshineradio.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:49:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sprint 1: simplify social publishing pipeline, remove
 Templated.io dependency

- Replace Templated.io dynamic image rendering with predefined local show
  visuals under media/shows/<slug>.<ext>, resolved via new
  showMediaResolver.js (program name -> slug -> local file + public URL).
- bufferPublisherService.publishToBuffer: mediaUrl is now optional; when
  absent, the post is sent text-only instead of blocking publication.
- socialPublishService.js rewritten around the simplified flow: resolve
  media -> build caption (hook + listening URL + hashtags) -> publish to
  Buffer -> notify Discord. No remote render/download step remains.
- New discordSocialNotifier.js: dedicated editorial-facing Discord
  notifications (publish success, publish failure, missing media asset),
  replacing the generic AlertManager system-alert webhook for this domain.
- playlist-update.js: passes the Discord gateway through to the social
  pipeline so it can send notifications; renamed the no-longer-accurate
  triggerSocialPlaceholder to triggerSocialPublish.
- config.js: removed TEMPLATED_* schema entries and hasTemplated(); added
  SOCIAL_SHOW_MEDIA_ROOT, SOCIAL_SHOW_MEDIA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL, and
  SOCIAL_NOTIFICATIONS_CHANNEL_ID (all optional, with sane defaults).
- Removed templatedClient.js and its test.
- Kept bufferPublisherService's GraphQL integration, socialPublishService
  as the orchestration entry point, and mediaStorageService.js (unused by
  this flow now, left untouched per sprint scope) as-is.
- Tests: rewrote api.socialPublishService.test.js for the new flow, added
  api.showMediaResolver.test.js and api.discordSocialNotifier.test.js,
  extended api.bufferPublisherService.test.js for the no-image case, and
  updated the two (identical, pre-existing duplicate) integration test
  files for the new gateway argument.
- docs: README.md env var section updated to match.
